9-28l-31-94c-6-15-23-28-40-28h-120c-55 0-100-45-100-100v-450c0-55 45-100 100-100h800c55 0 100 45 100 100v450c0 55-45 100-100 100z m-400-550c-138 0-250 112-250 250 0 138 112 250 250 250 138 0 250-112 250-250 0-138-112-250-250-250z m365 380c-19 0-35-16-35-35 0-19 16-35 35-35 19 0 35 16 35 35 0 19-16 35-35 35z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Open in dialog (edit layout)" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="M786 296v-267q0-15-11-26t-25-10h-214v214h-143v-214h-214q-15 0-25 10t-11 26v267q0 1 0 2t0 2l321 264 321-264q1-1 1-4z m124 39l-34-41q-5-5-12-6h-2q-7 0-12 3l-386 322-386-322q-7-4-13-4-7 2-12 7l-35 41q-4 5-3 13t6 12l401 334q18 15 42 15t43-15l136-114v109q0 8 5 13t13 5h107q8 0 13-5t5-13v-227l122-102q5-5 6-12t-4-13z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div></div></div><svg class="main-svg" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" width="542.3333333333334" height="310.6666666666667"><g class="hoverlayer"></g></svg></div></div></div></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(660,20)" x="660" y="20" title="codeHTML" width="560" height="332" class="codeHTML" name="codeHTML" rot="0"><foreignObject x="0" y="0" width="560" height="332" style="width: 560px; height: 332px;"><div name="htmlCode" style="zoom: 0.56; height: 592.857px; width: 1000px;" code="&lt;div class=&quot;ch&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Relaxation oscillator with a comparator&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How it works&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The output &lt;code&gt;out&lt;/code&gt; swings between &lt;strong&gt;Vol = &amp;minus;5 V&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Voh = +5 V&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;R&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;R2&lt;/strong&gt; bring a fraction &amp;beta; = R2/(R + R2) = 0.5 of the output back to the non-inverting input &lt;code&gt;p&lt;/code&gt; (positive feedback): the threshold is +2.5 V when the output is high and &amp;minus;2.5 V when it is low.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;R1&lt;/strong&gt; charges &lt;strong&gt;C1&lt;/strong&gt; from the output (negative feedback). When the voltage &lt;code&gt;n&lt;/code&gt; of the capacitor crosses the threshold on &lt;code&gt;p&lt;/code&gt;, the output flips and C1 starts to charge in the other direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Frequency&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;f = 1 / (2 &amp;middot; R1 &amp;middot; C1 &amp;middot; ln((1 + &amp;beta;)/(1 &amp;minus; &amp;beta;)))&lt;/code&gt; = 1 / (2 &amp;middot; 10 k&amp;Omega; &amp;middot; 100 nF &amp;middot; ln 3) &amp;asymp; 455 Hz (about 2.2 ms).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the PyAMS simulation the period is 2.2 ms. The first period is longer because the capacitor starts discharged.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Notes&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Not the usual drawing:&lt;/strong&gt; in the picture of a relaxation oscillator that is often shown, &lt;code&gt;R&lt;/code&gt; comes from the input terminal. Here &lt;code&gt;R&lt;/code&gt; comes from the &lt;strong&gt;output&lt;/strong&gt;, because without positive feedback there are no two thresholds and the circuit cannot oscillate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vol = &amp;minus;5 V:&lt;/strong&gt; with the default levels (0 V and 5 V) the lower threshold is 0 V and the capacitor, which discharges toward 0 V, never reaches it: the oscillation stops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vos = 1 mV:&lt;/strong&gt; the circuit is perfectly symmetric and would stay at 0 V; a small input offset gives the start (like the noise of a real circuit).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time domain analysis: 0 ... 10 ms with a step of 5 &amp;micro;s. Plotted: &lt;code&gt;out&lt;/code&gt;, the capacitor &lt;code&gt;n&lt;/code&gt; and the threshold &lt;code&gt;p&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
"> 
